- op: update  # d105
  at: '2026-05-17T20:51:51Z'  # d105
  by: agent  # d105
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d105
  clock: 25  # d105
  nonce: d105  # d105
  set:  # d105
    fields:  # d105
      root_cause: "Route detection has shipped four expansions since the original 2026-03-10 framing: JSX <Route path> detection (PR #2127), createBrowserRouter/createRoutesFromElements object configs with nested children (PR #2261), loader_ref/action_ref linking (PR #2295), and React.lazy() component detection (PR #2299). As of 2026-05-17 code review, the invariant is violated by five residual gaps: (1) <Route index> JSX shorthand without a path attribute is filtered out at js_ts.py:1011; (2) {index: true, ...} object-config sibling of (1) is filtered out at js_ts.py:1163; (3) v5 <Route render={...}> prop pattern is not recognized at js_ts.py:1008 (only element/component attrs handled); (4) <Route path={someVar}> JSX expression paths are silently skipped at js_ts.py:992-993 (attr_value only set from string nodes); (5) {path: someVar, ...} object-config dynamic paths emit FALSE-POSITIVE Route nodes with the identifier text as the bogus path at js_ts.py:1138-1140. Gap (5) is qualitatively worse than the silent-skip gaps because it produces junk entries in routes.txt rather than missing entries. Gaps (1)+(2) are the same v6 idiom in two syntactic surfaces and should be addressed together. Gaps (3)+(4) are corner cases in older or expression-built configs."  # d105
- op: discuss  # cb2d
  at: '2026-05-17T20:53:13Z'  # cb2d
  by: agent  # cb2d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cb2d
  clock: 26  # cb2d
  nonce: cb2d  # cb2d
  message: "Correction to my 2026-05-17T19:44:18Z migration note. That note claimed the remaining patterns were 'lazy routes via React.lazy + dynamic import, route loader/action detection.' That was wrong — both shipped in March 2026 (React.lazy in PR #2299, loader/action in PR #2295), ~24 hours after the 2026-03-16 human direction I was executing. I carried forward the pre-PR list without checking that the work had landed.\n\nThe verified-as-of-2026-05-17 remaining gaps are five (code-cited in fields.root_cause). Summary:\n\n(1) <Route index> JSX shorthand — coverage gap, modern v6 idiom\n(2) {index: true, ...} object-config sibling of (1) — same v6 idiom, object syntax\n(3) v5 <Route render={...}> prop — coverage gap, older idiom\n(4) <Route path={var}> JSX expression paths — silent skip, defensible\n(5) {path: someVar, ...} object-config dynamic paths — FALSE-POSITIVE EMITTER\n\nNote that gap (5) is qualitatively different from the other four. (1)-(4) are silent coverage gaps — they make routes invisible, which is the same failure mode the invariant was filed against. (5) emits Route nodes with bogus paths derived from identifier text — it puts garbage IN the routes output. Fix is small (~2 hr): at js_ts.py:1138-1140, check that value_node.type == 'string' before extracting; skip emission otherwise (matching the JSX-side behavior at gap #4).\n\nGaps (1)+(2) want to be addressed together — same v6 idiom, two syntactic surfaces. Resolution requires a design decision: what IS the path of an index route in routes.txt? Options: (a) inherit parent path, (b) parent path + '/<index>' marker, (c) emit with a meta key marking it as index. Should be settled before either gap is fixed in isolation, or the JSX and object-config sides will diverge.\n\nStatus stays violated (per 2026-03-16 direction: violated until all aspects hold). Priority stays P4 (corpus signal hasn't surfaced these gaps as user pain). Reopen as a fresh focused item if any of (1)-(5) gets active corpus signal; otherwise let the five sit on this item collectively."  # cb2d
- op: discuss  # 9ee3
  at: '2026-05-24T06:30:53Z'  # 9ee3
  by: agent  # 9ee3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9ee3
  clock: 27  # 9ee3
  nonce: 9ee3  # 9ee3
  message: "Partial closure: PR #3892 (21527cbba4) closes gaps (3), (4), (5) from the 2026-05-17 audit. Gap (5) — {path: someVar, ...} no longer emits junk routes (FP eliminated). Gap (4) — <Route path={var}> no longer emits junk routes (FP eliminated). Gap (3) — v5 <Route render={...}> now recognized for handler_ref. Status stays violated per 2026-03-16 discipline (held until all five aspects resolve). Remaining: gaps (1) JSX <Route index> and (2) {index: true, ...} object-config index routes — both still need the routes.txt output-shape design call documented in fields.root_cause (options a/b/c). Reopen as a focused item if either gap surfaces in bakeoff or UAT signal; otherwise let them sit on this item collectively."  # 9ee3
